    <div class="story" id="tl">
      <span class="comet" aria-hidden="true"><i class="tail"></i><i class="head"></i></span>
      <article class="chapter rv">
        <span class="ch-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ch-photo">
          <figure class="ch-main photo-card tl-l"><div class="pc-in"><img src="/gal/socal-showdown-2025/06.webp" alt="The whole team outside with The Golden Griffins banner at SoCal Showdown 2025" loading="lazy"></div></figure>
          <figure class="ch-second"><span class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></span><img src="/gal/beach-blitz-2024/03.webp" alt="Team members cheering in the stands with a 6220 sign at Beach Blitz 2024" loading="lazy"></figure>
          <p class="ch-cap">SoCal Showdown · 2025</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-body"><span class="ch-yr">2024–2026</span><h3>Building a system</h3><p>The team grew from about a dozen students to nearly 50. We moved to swerve drive and camera-based autonomous driving, started a fall training boot camp and a student-run summer camp, and began writing down how we do things. In 2026, our first season in the new <i>FIRST</i> California district, we placed 3rd at the Los Angeles District Event, were a first pick at the Orange County District Event, and qualified for the Southern State Championship.</p><div class="learned"><p class="eyebrow">What we learned</p><ul><li>Growing fast needs structure: clear roles, training and documentation.</li><li>A pre-match checklist is part of the robot. In 2026 it kept us on the field.</li><li>Next: more mentors, better task tracking, and wiring that never comes loose.</li></ul></div><ul class="badges" aria-label="Awards and milestones"><li class="wbadge"><span class="wing wing-l" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span><span>State Championship 2026</span><span class="wing wing-r" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span></li></ul><a class="ch-link" href="/resources/media#socal-showdown-2025">See photos →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="chapter flip rv">
        <span class="ch-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ch-photo">
          <figure class="ch-main photo-card"><div class="pc-in"><img src="/gal/oc-regional-2022/07.webp" alt="Team members in masks posing in the pits in 2022" loading="lazy"></div></figure>
          <figure class="ch-second"><span class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></span><img src="/gal/beach-blitz-2022/09.webp" alt="The team celebrating together after Beach Blitz 2022" loading="lazy"></figure>
          <p class="ch-cap">OC Regional · 2022</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-body"><span class="ch-yr">2020–2023</span><h3>Starting over</h3><p>COVID-19 closed our shop, most of our mentors moved on, and our older design files were lost. A small group of students kept the team going online. In 2022 students secured our first dedicated shop in the new STEM building, and that fall we earned the Against All Odds Award at Beach Blitz. In 2023, now named the Golden Griffins, we were Regional Finalists at the Orange County Regional.</p><div class="learned"><p class="eyebrow">What we learned</p><ul><li>A team can run on student leadership. This is where "student-led, student-driven" comes from.</li><li>Keep everything in the cloud (CAD in Onshape, chat in Discord) so knowledge outlasts every graduating class.</li><li>Set up the shop before build season, not during it.</li></ul></div><ul class="badges" aria-label="Awards and milestones"><li class="wbadge"><span class="wing wing-l" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span><span>Against All Odds 2022</span><span class="wing wing-r" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span></li><li class="wbadge"><span class="wing wing-l" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span><span>Finalist 2023</span><span class="wing wing-r" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span></li></ul><a class="ch-link" href="/resources/media#oc-regional-2022">See photos →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="chapter rv">
        <span class="ch-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ch-photo">
          <figure class="ch-main photo-card tl-l"><div class="pc-in"><img src="/gal/power-up-2018/01.webp" alt="The 2018 team photo in the school parking lot" loading="lazy"></div></figure>
          <figure class="ch-second is-render"><span class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></span><img src="/assets/main/fc1361c0d9.webp" alt="CAD render of the 2019 robot" loading="lazy"></figure>
          <p class="ch-cap">The 2018 team · 2019 robot</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-body"><span class="ch-yr">2017–2019</span><h3>Learning the hard way</h3><p>We competed at the Orange County Regional every year and added Beach Blitz in 2018 and 2019, where we were an alliance captain in 2018. These seasons taught us most of the engineering rules we still follow, usually by breaking them first.</p><div class="learned"><p class="eyebrow">What we learned</p><ul><li>Use proven off-the-shelf parts unless we can machine something precisely.</li><li>Test every mechanism on the bench before it goes on the robot, and track weight in CAD from day one.</li><li>Wire for reliability. One loose connector can stop a whole robot.</li></ul></div><ul class="badges" aria-label="Awards and milestones"><li class="wbadge"><span class="wing wing-l" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span><span>Alliance Captain 2018</span><span class="wing wing-r" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span></li></ul><a class="ch-link" href="/resources/media#power-up-2018">See photos →</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="chapter flip rv">
        <span class="ch-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="ch-photo">
          <figure class="ch-main photo-card"><div class="pc-in"><img src="/gal/stronghold-2016/01.webp" alt="Team members holding the FIRST Robotics Competition Winner banner in 2016" loading="lazy"></div></figure>
          <figure class="ch-second"><span class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></span><img src="/gal/stronghold-2016/03.webp" alt="Teams gathered on the field at the 2016 World Championship" loading="lazy"></figure>
          <p class="ch-cap">OC Regional Winner · 2016</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-body"><span class="ch-yr">2016</span><h3>Founding</h3><p>About ten Los Alamitos High School students started the team, working out of the Build-It Workspace with seed money from Boeing and the Build It initiative. In our rookie season we won the Orange County Regional as part of the first-seeded alliance and went to the World Championship in St. Louis.</p><div class="learned"><p class="eyebrow">What we learned</p><ul><li>A simple robot that works beats an ambitious one that isn't finished.</li><li>Have your tools and spare parts organized before you get to the event.</li></ul></div><ul class="badges" aria-label="Awards and milestones"><li class="wbadge"><span class="wing wing-l" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span><span>Regional Winner</span><span class="wing wing-r" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span></li><li class="wbadge"><span class="wing wing-l" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span><span>World Championship</span><span class="wing wing-r" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#wing"/></svg></span></li></ul><a class="ch-link" href="/resources/media#stronghold-2016">See photos →</a></div>
      </article>
